	(text "COMPUTE (record section 8; SPEC: no RP2350, the P4 LP core emits quadrature). Stamp-P4 + Stamp-AddOn C6 stacked on top (SDIO G42-G48, not castellated).\nFixed pins only: VIN (14) from +5V, the stamp ORs it with its own USB-C 5V and makes SOC_3.3V itself; all GND pads; CHIP_EN + G35 buttons (stamp has 10k pull-ups).\nG35 appears on pads 36 AND 48 in M5's own symbol and schematic: both wired to P4_BOOT.\nPIN ASSIGNMENT FOLLOWS LAYOUT (operator ruling): each function net below gets the stamp pad nearest its circuit once parts are placed.\n  QUAD_A, QUAD_B          LP GPIO (LPG0-15) for the LP-core emitter; avoid LPG14/15 (LP UART console)\n  I2C_SDA, I2C_SCL        LPG11 / LPG9 are the module I2C (shared with the add-on connector; SPEC open item)\n  RS485_TX, RS485_RX, RS485_DE   any HP GPIO via the matrix (UART RS485 half-duplex mode)\n  MOTOR_EN, PRECHARGE_EN, MSW_FLT_N, INA_ALERT_N, CLAMP_MON, DRV_ALM, DRV_RDY, DRV_ZO, FAN_PWM, FAN_TACH, LED_DATA\n  MSW_IMON, THERM          ADC1 (G16-G23)\n  Avoid straps: G34 (JTAG enable), G35 (boot), G36, G37/G38 (UART0 console).\nD5: one status pixel for Flux. 3.3 V data into a 5 V WS2812B is marginal: TODO(detailing) pick a 3.3 V-tolerant pixel or level-shift through a spare AHCT125 gate."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
